{"packet_id":"D076-01","doc_id":"D076","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"pending_bill","title":"Proposed ban on anti-competitive automated rent price-fixing","requirement":"A person may not sell, license or provide an algorithmic device to a landlord, and a landlord may not use an algorithmic device to set rental rates or occupancy levels for residential rental property.","key_value":"$1,000 per violation","coverage_conditions":"Applies citywide to landlords and to persons who sell, license or provide algorithmic devices for residential rental property in the City of San Diego.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rental property in the City of San Diego"},"exemptions":"Software that publishes reports from aggregated nonpublic competitor data more than 90 days old or from public information and does not recommend future rental rates or occupancy levels; software used to establish rental rates or income limits under local, state or federal affordable housing program guidelines.","penalty":"Tenant may seek injunctive relief, damages, or civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation; a prevailing tenant recovers costs and reasonable attorney's fees, and lease provisions limiting such fees are unenforceable.","effective_date":null,"citation":"San Diego Mun. Code § 98.1103","quoted_span":"(a) It is unlawful for a person to sell, license, or otherwise provide an
algorithmic device to a landlord.
(b) It is unlawful for a landlord to use an algorithmic device to set rental rates
or occupancy levels for residential rental property.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":true,"conflict_note":"The ordinance takes effect on the thirtieth day after final passage, but the packet leaves the final passage date blank, so no effective date can be stated.","n_rules":1}
